// PARAM: --analysis interval --solver join
// The precision ceiling of the two-origin slot the widening rules are
// compared against. p's single FunctionEntry seed is written by two call
// sites, [1,1] and [2,2]; join accumulates them into the slot without ever
// widening, so the entry value is exactly [1,2] and n < 10 is decided.
//
// Same program as known-imprecision/03-warrow_joins_before_widening.vimp
// (warrow, [1,+inf]) and precision/06-warrow_per_origin_keeps_bound.vimp
// (warrow-per-origin, [1,2]): join has no termination guarantee on a
// growing chain but loses nothing here, and warrow-per-origin meets this
// same value while keeping that guarantee.
void p(int32 n) {
  __voblint_check(n < 10) // PROVED
}
void main() {
  p(1);
  p(2)
}
